,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":439.385825241,"data":"    \"output\": \"\u003cthink\u003e\\nWe are given the exact evidence: \\n  - \\\"Rows increase toward the south and columns increase toward the east.\\\"\\n  - \\\"I applied A3. A color-2 cell left row 4 column 4 and appeared at row 4 column 5.\\\"\\n  - \\\"No other persistent cell changed. The environment did not report success.\\\"\\n\\nWe are to infer the meaning of the action \\\"A3\\\". The action is applied to a cell (row4, col4) and then the cell moves to (row4, col5). \\n\\nGiven the grid layout: \\n  - Rows increase toward the south. So row 1 is north, row 2 is north of row 3? Actually, if rows increase toward the south, then row 1 is the northernmost and row n is the southernmost. \\n  - Columns increase toward the east, so column 1 is west and column n is east.\\n\\nIn\",\n"}
